(211,NULL,'RELATIONSHIP_SOCIAL','CLASSIC_COMMON','EN','KR',48,'a sight for sore eyes','보기만 해도 반가운 사람/것','반가움을 표현하는 a sight for sore eyes','직역하면 ''아픈 눈에 좋은 광경'', 즉 ''보기만 해도 반가운 사람/것''이라는 뜻입니다. 오랜만에 만난 사람이나 간절히 기다리던 것에 쓰는 유쾌한 표현이에요.','It''s been years! How are you?','이게 얼마 만이야! 어떻게 지냈어?','Look who''s here! You''re a sight for sore eyes!','이게 누구야! 얼굴 보니까 너무 반갑다!',ARRAY['Look','who''s','here','You''re','a','sight','for','sore','eyes']::varchar[],ARRAY['Look','eye','sights','of','who''s','sight','You''re','here','eyes','a','sore','for']::varchar[],NULL,'[{"sentenceText": "After that long hike, the hotel was a sight for sore eyes.", "highlightingPart": "a sight for sore eyes", "sentenceTranslation": "긴 등산 끝에 호텔이 어찌나 반갑던지.", "practiceQuestion": "How was the trail? I heard it''s brutal.", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "등산로 어땠어? 엄청 힘들다던데.", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/211/practice-examples/a49574bb-cc0c-4a04-bd31-b8f5797b3037.webp", "sentenceWords": ["After", "that", "long", "hike", "the", "hotel", "was", "a", "sight", "for", "sore", "eyes"], "sentenceWordChoices": ["hike", "long", "sight", "eye", "the", "of", "eyes", "a", "sights", "that", "for", "was", "After", "hotel", "sore"]}, {"sentenceText": "Aren''t you a sight for sore eyes! It''s been years!", "highlightingPart": "a sight for sore eyes", "sentenceTranslation": "이게 얼마 만이야, 얼굴 보니 진짜 반갑다!", "practiceQuestion": "Hey, remember me? We worked together back in the day.", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "야, 나 기억나? 우리 옛날에 같이 일했잖아.", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/211/practice-examples/91de6e79-1cbe-47df-b740-799f5157cacb.webp", "sentenceWords": ["Aren''t", "you", "a", "sight", "for", "sore", "eyes", "It''s", "been", "years"], "sentenceWordChoices": ["of", "for", "sights", "been", "you", "sore", "eyes", "a", "sight", "Aren''t", "sour", "years", "It''s"]}, {"sentenceText": "That cup of coffee was a sight for sore eyes this morning.", "highlighti