(247,NULL,'OPINION_JUDGMENT','BASIC','EN','KR',84,'miss out on','(좋은 기회를) 놓치다','기회를 놓치지 않는 miss out on','''(좋은 기회를) 놓치다''라는 뜻입니다. 단순히 miss보다 ''누릴 수 있었던 것을 놓친 아쉬움''이 강조되고, FOMO(fear of missing out)의 어원이기도 해요.','The sale ends today, you know.','세일 오늘 끝나는 거 알지?','Don''t miss out on the sale!','세일 놓치지 마!',ARRAY['Don''t','miss','out','on','the','sale']::varchar[],ARRAY['misses','Don''t','in','sale','miss','sell','on','the','out']::varchar[],NULL,'[{"sentenceText": "I missed out on the concert tickets.", "highlightingPart": "missed out on", "sentenceTranslation": "콘서트 표를 놓쳤어.", "practiceQuestion": "Weren''t you going to see that band next month?", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "너 다음 달에 그 밴드 보러 간다고 하지 않았어?", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/247/practice-examples/2ef9a5ef-e56a-4d38-a6ae-420b0ad8ba82.webp", "sentenceWords": ["I", "missed", "out", "on", "the", "concert", "tickets"], "sentenceWordChoices": ["on", "in", "concert", "miss", "tickets", "concerts", "the", "out", "I", "missed"]}, {"sentenceText": "You''re missing out on so much fun!", "highlightingPart": "missing out on", "sentenceTranslation": "너 이 재미를 놓치고 있는 거야!", "practiceQuestion": "I think I''ll just stay home tonight.", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "난 그냥 오늘 밤 집에 있을래.", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/247/practice-examples/24afb891-6d16-4f04-ba17-8b6a3295ee6e.webp", "sentenceWords": ["You''re", "missing", "out", "on", "so", "much", "fun"], "sentenceWordChoices": ["so", "Your", "You''re", "many", "fun", "out", "missing", "much", "on", "miss"]}, {"sentenceText": "Sign up early so you don''t miss out.", "highlightingPart": "miss out", "sentenceTranslation": "놓치지 않게 일찍 신청해.", "practiceQuestion": "When should I register for the workshop?", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "워크숍 언제 등록해야 해?", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/247/practice-examples/19de6990-a0e1-4915-8945-5c9e0879fd4c.webp", "sentenceWords"