(252,NULL,'WORK_STUDY','BASIC','EN','KR',89,'get around to','(미뤄왔던 일을) 마침내 하다','미루다 결국 하는 get around to','''(미뤄왔던 일을) 마침내 하다''라는 뜻입니다. 바빠서 못 하고 있던 일에 드디어 손을 댄다는 뉘앙스로, to 뒤에 명사나 동명사가 와요.','Did you ever clean your room?','방 청소 결국 했어?','I finally got around to cleaning my room.','드디어 방 청소를 하게 됐어.',ARRAY['I','finally','got','around','to','cleaning','my','room']::varchar[],ARRAY['to','finally','cleaning','I','got','room','clean','get','my','around','mine']::varchar[],NULL,'[{"sentenceText": "I''ll get around to it this weekend.", "highlightingPart": "get around to", "sentenceTranslation": "이번 주말엔 그거 할게.", "practiceQuestion": "That closet still needs organizing, you know.", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "그 옷장 아직 정리해야 하는 거 알지?", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/252/practice-examples/5ae181b8-d3d7-4c46-8f8a-ec064255ba53.webp", "sentenceWords": ["I''ll", "get", "around", "to", "it", "this", "weekend"], "sentenceWordChoices": ["gets", "it", "get", "to", "weekend", "its", "I''ll", "around", "weekends", "this"]}, {"sentenceText": "She never got around to reading that book.", "highlightingPart": "got around to", "sentenceTranslation": "걔는 결국 그 책을 못 읽었어.", "practiceQuestion": "Did she like the novel you lent her?", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "네가 빌려준 소설 걔 좋아했어?", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/252/practice-examples/ff918606-60aa-4d45-a73c-f6f1f1c77d17.webp", "sentenceWords": ["She", "never", "got", "around", "to", "reading", "that", "book"], "sentenceWordChoices": ["around", "to", "get", "got", "book", "She", "books", "never", "read", "reading", "that"]}, {"sentenceText": "When are you going to get around to fixing the door?", "highlightingPart": "get around to", "sentenceTranslation": "문은 대체 언제 고칠 거야?", "practiceQuestion": "Ugh, this door handle came off in my hand again.", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "아, 이 문손잡이 또 빠졌어.", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/252/