(361,NULL,'DAILY_ROUTINE','CLASSIC_COMMON','EN','KR',198,'head out','이만 나서다, 출발하다','자리 뜰 때 쓰는 head out','모임이나 자리에서 슬슬 일어날 때 "I''m gonna head out"이라고 하면 leave보다 부드럽고 자연스럽게 들린다. 어디로 출발한다는 의미로도 폭넓게 쓰여서, 약속 장소로 나설 때도 그대로 쓸 수 있다.','Are you leaving already?','벌써 가는 거야?','Yeah, I''m gonna head out. It''s getting late.','응, 이만 가볼게. 시간이 늦었네.',ARRAY['Yeah','I''m','gonna','head','out','It''s','getting','late']::varchar[],ARRAY['head','Yeah','gonna','It''s','getting','get','lately','heads','out','I''m','late']::varchar[],NULL,'[{"sentenceText": "Let''s head out around eight.", "highlightingPart": "head out", "sentenceTranslation": "8시쯤 출발하자.", "practiceQuestion": "What time do we need to leave tomorrow?", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "내일 우리 몇 시에 나가야 돼?", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/361/practice-examples/3d4fc243-0b07-4694-a907-075f9ee9bd56.webp", "sentenceWords": ["Let''s", "head", "out", "around", "eight"], "sentenceWordChoices": ["out", "eight", "around", "heads", "head", "eights", "Let''s"]}, {"sentenceText": "He headed out like ten minutes ago.", "highlightingPart": "headed out", "sentenceTranslation": "걔 10분 전쯤 나갔어.", "practiceQuestion": "Where''s Marco? I don''t see him anywhere.", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "마르코 어디 갔어? 안 보이네.", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/361/practice-examples/6269cc7e-cc49-4370-b40e-a525cdb9cbba.webp", "sentenceWords": ["He", "headed", "out", "like", "ten", "minutes", "ago"], "sentenceWordChoices": ["minute", "minutes", "like", "ten", "He", "headed", "out", "ago", "head"]}, {"sentenceText": "I''m heading out early. I have class at nine.", "highlightingPart": "heading out", "sentenceTranslation": "일찍 나가려고. 9시에 수업 있거든.", "practiceQuestion": "You''re packing up your stuff already?", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "벌써 짐 챙기는 거야?", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/361/practice-examples/884bc27e-e7e0-42b6-8ba6-6a955214bab9.webp", "s