(861,NULL,'OPINION_JUDGMENT','CLASSIC_COMMON','EN','KR',698,'pan out','(일이) 잘 풀리다, 결실을 보다','일이 잘 풀리다 pan out','계획이나 시도가 결국 잘 풀렸는지 아닌지를 말할 때 쓰는 표현이다. 사금 채취에서 접시(pan)를 흔들어 금이 나오는지 보던 데서 온 말로, "it didn''t pan out"처럼 부정형으로 결과를 회고할 때 특히 자주 쓰인다. 캐주얼한 대화부터 회사 얘기까지 두루 어울리는 중립적인 표현이다.','Whatever happened to your food truck idea?','너 푸드트럭 하겠다던 건 어떻게 됐어?','It didn''t pan out, so I''m back to job hunting.','잘 안 풀려서 다시 구직 중이야.',ARRAY['It','didn''t','pan','out','so','I''m','back','to','job','hunting']::varchar[],ARRAY['back','didn''t','out','panned','pan','doesn''t','hunt','I''m','job','It','to','hunting','so']::varchar[],NULL,'[{"sentenceText": "Yeah, it actually panned out better than I expected.", "highlightingPart": "panned out", "sentenceTranslation": "응, 생각보다 훨씬 잘 풀렸어.", "practiceQuestion": "Did the study group thing work out?", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "그 스터디 그룹은 잘 됐어?", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/861/practice-examples/6694beae-a90f-4120-bcf7-ad6e24bfd39f.webp", "sentenceWords": ["Yeah", "it", "actually", "panned", "out", "better", "than", "I", "expected"], "sentenceWordChoices": ["panned", "Yeah", "then", "I", "out", "actually", "best", "than", "expected", "better", "pan", "it"]}, {"sentenceText": "The job over there just didn''t pan out.", "highlightingPart": "pan out", "sentenceTranslation": "거기 일이 그냥 잘 안 풀렸어.", "practiceQuestion": "Why did you move back from Sydney?", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "시드니에서 왜 다시 돌아온 거야?", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/861/practice-examples/63c4c907-5f21-464d-b0c3-4e47a15aa226.webp", "sentenceWords": ["The", "job", "over", "there", "just", "didn''t", "pan", "out"], "sentenceWordChoices": ["job", "The", "just", "pan", "panned", "over", "didn''t", "there", "their", "out", "doesn''t"]}, {"sentenceText": "We''ll see how it pans out this semester.", "highlightingPart": "pans out", "sentenceTranslation": "이번 학기에 어떻게 되는지 보려고.", "practiceQuestion": "Are you still doing that side project with Marco?", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "마르코랑 하던 그 사이드 프로젝트 아직 해?", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/861/practice-examples/586dfbc8-d761-47b4-b54e-77c76b9ec7b6.webp", "sentenceWords": ["We''ll", "see", "how", "it", "pans", "out", "this", "semester"], "sentenceWordChoices": ["how", "pan", "this", "it", "sees", "see", "semester", "that", "pans", "We''ll", "out"]}, {"sentenceText": "Surprisingly, it panned out great — the place was spotless.", "highlightingPart": "panned out", "sentenceTranslation": "의외로 대성공이었어, 완전 깨끗하더라.", "practiceQuestion": "Was booking the cheap hostel a good call?", "practiceQuestionTranslation": "그 싸구려 호스텔 예약한 거 잘한 선택이었어?", "imageUrl": "https://d19azau1un4t7r.cloudfront.net/content/expressions/861/practice-examples/3f5a4dcf-96bd-4023-b74d-c871b613f4a2.webp", "sentenceWords": ["Surprisingly", "it", "panned", "out", "great", "the", "place", "was", "spotless"], "sentenceWordChoices": ["it", "panned", "were", "was", "spotless", "out", "place", "Surprisingly", "greatly", "the", "pan", "great"]}]'::jsonb,'FREE_TALK','ACTIVE',now(),now(),'[-0.00381278992,-0.0242156982,-0.045715332,0.0117797852,-0.0399475098,0.00666427612,-0.0133743286,-0.0100402832,-0.0102157593,0.0105285645,0.0238189697,0.0156402588,0.0440063477,0.00708770752,0.0343017578,0.000710964203,-0.058013916,0.0426025391,0.0213470459,0.0201873779,-0.00305747986,-0.0331115723,0.00312995911,0.0311737061,-0.0213470459,0.00580215454,0.00137424469,0.0248565674,0.0596008301,0.0111618042,0.00262069702,-0.0429077148,0.0325317383,-0.0552368164,-0.00936126709,0.0203704834,-0.00227165222,0.00441741943,-0.0340270996,-0.0124282837,0.0720214844,-0.00449752808,0.0138092041,-0.0138015747,0.0886230469,0.051361084,-0.00010663271,0.0493774414,0.0353088379,0.0183258057,-0.00840759277,0.0262145996,0.016204834,0.0190887451,0.00550842285,-8.1717968e-05,0.015586853,0.0165863037,0.0362854004,-0.00468826294,0.0489501953,-0.0122299194,0.0681152344,